10. Install and Explore Selenium for Automated Testing
1. What is Selenium?
- Selenium is an open-source tool used to automate web browsers.
- It is used for testing web applications automatically without manual interaction.
- It supports programming languages like Java, Python, and JavaScript.
- It supports browsers like Chrome, Firefox, and Edge.
2. Selenium Installation (Windows)
Step 1: Install Python

Check whether Python is installed:
python --version


Step 2: Install Selenium

Open CMD or VS Code terminal:
pip install selenium


Step 3: Verify installation
pip show selenium


Step 4: Install Google Chrome

Install Chrome if it is not already available.

Note: Modern Selenium includes Selenium Manager, which can automatically manage the required browser driver.
3. Explore Selenium Environment
Create a Python file named test.py.
from selenium import webdriverdriver = webdriver.Chrome()driver.get("https://www.google.com")print(driver.title)driver.quit()



Output:
Google


Explanation:
- webdriver.Chrome() – Opens Chrome browser.
- driver.get() – Opens the specified website.
- driver.title – Retrieves the webpage title.
- driver.quit() – Closes the browser.
4. Example: Automated Testing
Create an HTML file named index.html.
<html>
<body>
    <h2>Login Page</h2>

    <input id="username" placeholder="Username">
    <button id="login">Login</button>

    <p id="result"></p>

    <script>
        document.getElementById("login").onclick = function() {
            document.getElementById("result").innerHTML =
                "Login Successful";
        };
    </script>
</body>
</html>


Create test.py:
from selenium import webdriverfrom selenium.webdriver.common.by import Bydriver = webdriver.Chrome()driver.get("file:///D:/vs_codes/myjava/index.html")driver.find_element(By.ID, "username").send_keys("admin")driver.find_element(By.ID, "login").click()result = driver.find_element(By.ID, "result").textif result == "Login Successful":    print("Test Passed")else:    print("Test Failed")driver.quit()



Output:
Test Passed


5. Important Selenium Commands
Command	Purpose
webdriver.Chrome()	Opens Chrome
driver.get(url)	Opens a website
driver.title	Gets page title
driver.current_url	Gets current URL
find_element()	Finds an HTML element
send_keys()	Enters text
click()	Clicks an element
clear()	Clears input
driver.quit()	Closes browser

6. Advantages of Selenium
1. Reduces manual testing effort.
2. Supports multiple browsers and programming languages.
3. Helps identify errors in web applications.
4. Supports automated and repeated testing.
